<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Bitcoin</dt><dd>An open monetary network and asset governed by independently verified consensus rules.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Bitcoin history</dt><dd>The documented development of Bitcoin from its prehistory and launch through later technical, economic, and cultural milestones.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Open-Source development</dt><dd>The public process of proposing, reviewing, testing, maintaining, and distributing software whose source code can be inspected and modified.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Digital signature</dt><dd>Cryptographic proof that a valid private key authorized a transaction or message.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Validation</dt><dd>The process of checking transactions and blocks against applicable rules.</dd></div></dl></section>
